INSERT INTO forum_posts (category_id, title, body, author_name, pinned, published, published_at)
SELECT id, 'Start Here: Joining OVERTHRONE', '## Start Here
OVERTHRONE is a modded Minecraft server (NeoForge 1.21.1, around 100 mods). You need the modpack to join, as a normal Minecraft client can''t connect.

- **1. Get the modpack** Download the OVERTHRONE modpack and import it into your launcher (CurseForge, Prism or the Modrinth app). The download link is posted in our Discord.
- **2. Give Minecraft enough memory** In your launcher, set the memory (RAM) for the pack to **6–8 GB**. Less than that causes lag spikes and crashes with this many mods.
- **3. Join the server** Add a server with the address **overthronesmp.net** and join. The first load takes a while because of the mods. That''s normal.
- **4. Fix your keybinds** Several mods share the same default keys. Spend two minutes on the [keybind fixes](/guide#keybinds) before you fight anything.
- **5. Read the rules** Short version: no cheats, no griefing, be decent. Full list on the [rules page](/rules).
- **6. Link your Discord** In our Discord, run **/link** with your Minecraft name while you''re online in-game. You''ll get a 6-digit code in Minecraft chat. Then run **/verify** with that code in Discord.

## Your First Hour
A quick route through the server so you know where everything is.

- **1. Explore the hub** You spawn in the OVERTHRONE hub, a city above the clouds. The warp boards there list every destination, or type **/warp hub** to come back any time.
- **2. Go to the RPG world** Type **/rpg**. The RPG world is a protected city where nobody can break or place blocks. It holds the Quest Board, the Arcade & Trade Hall and the Arcanum.
- **3. Talk to Questmaster Orin** Right-click Orin in the RPG world to open the quest book. You can also open it with the quest book button in your inventory. Start with the first quests to earn coins and gear.
- **4. Visit the Arcade** Type **/warp arcade** to see the gacha machines, the vending machines and the exchange counter. Everything there is paid for with coins you earn in game.
- **5. Pick a home** Head to the survival world with **/warp survival**, find a spot and claim it with Open Parties and Claims (press **''**, the apostrophe key) so nobody can grief it.

[Open the full Player Guide](/guide#start)', 'OVERTHRONE Staff', 1, 1, strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
FROM forum_categories
WHERE slug = 'guides'
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM forum_posts WHERE title = 'Start Here: Joining OVERTHRONE');
INSERT INTO forum_posts (category_id, title, body, author_name, pinned, published, published_at)
SELECT id, 'Keybinds & Fixing Key Conflicts', '## Keybinds
These are the default keys for the main mods. Change any of them in Options → Controls → Key Binds. If your modpack already came with different keys, use those.

**Epic Fight (combat)**
- **R**: Switch between battle mode and mining mode
- **Left Mouse**: Attack (in battle mode)
- **Right Mouse**: Guard / block
- **Left Alt**: Dodge
- **Space**: Movement skill (for example a double jump), when you have one equipped
- **Left Mouse**: Weapon skill. It shares the attack button by default; many players move it to a mouse side button
- **G**: Lock on to a target
- **← / →**: Switch lock-on target
- **Middle Mouse**: Move the lock-on freely
- **K**: Skill menu (equip and upgrade skills)
- **Y**: Emote wheel

**Iron''s Spells ''n Spellbooks (magic)**
- **R**: Spell wheel: pick a spell from your spellbook
- **V**: Cast the selected spell
- **Left Alt + Scroll**: Scroll through the spell bar
- **Not set**: Quick-cast slots 1–15: bind these if you use a lot of spells

**Maps, waypoints and claims**
- **M**: Xaero''s World Map
- **Y**: Xaero''s Minimap settings
- **B**: Xaero''s: add a waypoint
- **U**: Xaero''s: waypoint list
- **M**: FTB Chunks map (the pack has both map mods)
- **'' (apostrophe)**: Open Parties and Claims menu: claims, parties and settings

**Voice chat, backpacks and other mods**
- **V**: Simple Voice Chat menu (proximity voice)
- **M**: Mute your microphone
- **N**: Turn voice chat off/on
- **H**: Hide voice chat icons
- **G**: Voice chat groups
- **B**: Open your Sophisticated Backpack
- **Alt + Z / Alt + X**: Toggle backpack upgrades 1 and 2
- **R / U**: JEI: recipes / uses of the item under your mouse (in inventories)
- **O**: Iris: choose a shader pack
- **K**: Iris: turn shaders on/off
- **R**: Iris: reload shaders

**Tensura: Reincarnated** and other mods add their own keys for skills and menus. Open Options → Controls → Key Binds and look through the Tensura categories.

## Fix Key Conflicts
With the default keys, one button does several things at once. For example, R switches Epic Fight mode, opens the spell wheel and reloads shaders. Here''s a setup that fixes all of them.

- **R**: change **Iron''s Spells: Spell Wheel** to **Z** (shared by Epic Fight mode switch · Iron''s spell wheel · Iris reload shaders)
- **R**: unbind **Iris: Reload Shaders**
- **V**: change **Iron''s Spells: Cast Spell** to **X or a mouse side button** (shared by Iron''s cast spell · Voice chat menu)
- **K**: unbind **Iris: Toggle Shaders** (use O instead) (shared by Epic Fight skill menu · Iris toggle shaders)
- **M**: unbind **FTB Chunks: Map** (use Xaero''s) (shared by Xaero''s World Map · FTB Chunks map · Voice chat mute)
- **M**: change **Voice Chat: Mute Microphone** to **J**
- **G**: unbind **Voice Chat: Groups** (groups are in the V menu) (shared by Epic Fight lock-on · Voice chat groups)
- **B**: unbind **Xaero''s: New Waypoint** (add waypoints from the map) (shared by Backpack · Xaero''s add waypoint)
- **Y**: unbind **Xaero''s: Minimap Settings** (shared by Epic Fight emotes · Xaero''s minimap settings)

Conflicting keys show in red in Options → Controls → Key Binds. If a button suddenly does two things, check there first.

[Open the full Player Guide](/guide#keybinds)', 'OVERTHRONE Staff', 1, 1, strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
FROM forum_categories
WHERE slug = 'guides'
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM forum_posts WHERE title = 'Keybinds & Fixing Key Conflicts');
INSERT INTO forum_posts (category_id, title, body, author_name, pinned, published, published_at)
SELECT id, 'Combat, Magic & Skills', '## Combat, Magic & Skills
Fighting on OVERTHRONE uses Epic Fight, so it plays very differently from vanilla Minecraft.

- **Battle mode vs mining mode.** Press **R** to swap. Battle mode gives you combos, guarding and dodging with weapons. Mining mode is normal Minecraft for building and digging.
- **Dodge, don''t tank.** **Left Alt** dodges through attacks. Big bosses hit hard, so learn their patterns and dodge their big swings.
- **Guard** with **Right Mouse**. Blocking at the right moment is much better than eating hits.
- **Weapon skills.** Each weapon type has its own skill and combo. Weapons from Weapons of Miracles and Simply Swords have special movesets.
- **Skill menu (K).** Equip skills like dodges and passives, and grow them with the Epic Fight Skill Tree.
- **Magic.** Iron''s Spells ''n Spellbooks adds spellbooks, scrolls and mana. Put spells into your spellbook at an Inscription Table, choose one with the spell wheel and cast it.
- **Tensura: Reincarnated** is the core of the server: your race, unique and extra skills, magic and battlewills. Browse them on the [Tensura Skills](/tensura) page.
- **Classes.** Visit **/warp classes** in the hub to see the classes.

Damage numbers (from Combat Numbers) pop up when you hit something, so you can see which weapon and skills actually do more damage.

[Open the full Player Guide](/guide#combat)', 'OVERTHRONE Staff', 0, 1, strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', 'now')
FROM forum_categories
WHERE slug = 'guides'
  AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM forum_posts WHERE title = 'Combat, Magic & Skills');
